{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to 2d2c650f, LS-3: the classifier in the scripts only, as\nyou recommend.\n\nNo typed `TransportError` goes through the CLI `Outcome`. A wider\nSDK surface for one red workflow costs more than it gives, and the\nsource shows no product fault yet.\n\n1. Extend the list of LS-2 with the closed kinds of transport\n   failure and the status class of a reply.\n2. Capture the lifecycle of the proxy and the Worker, the last\n   startup status and sessions observation, and the class of the\n   install exchange, before cleanup. Each one comes from a closed\n   list.\n3. The existing witness drives the real planned CLI with the five\n   replies that you name, and it holds the exact names, the\n   absence of the sentinel and the kept custody of the attempt.\n4. The head joins the next gate after CE-2, or takes its own.\n\nMake this run decide the owner of the fault. If two classes can\nstill explain one output line, add the field that separates them\nnow. A third red run that names no owner costs one more landing.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}